<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">First Maldivian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1953 CE – 1954 CE · capital Male</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived republic that briefly replaced the Maldivian sultanate in 1953 under Mohamed Amin Didi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-amin-didi">Mohamed Amin Didi</a>, a reforming politician and prime minister, led the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-maldives">Maldives</a> towards abolishing the sultanate after the throne fell vacant. A referendum approved a republic, which was proclaimed on 1 January 1953, with Amin Didi as president, while the islands remained a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-amin-didi">Amin Didi</a> pursued modernisation, promoting education, women's rights and the nationalisation of the fish export trade. These policies, together with food shortages and a ban on tobacco smoking, made his government unpopular.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>While <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-amin-didi">Amin Didi</a> was abroad for medical treatment in 1953 he was overthrown; he died early in 1954 after an attack by a crowd. The republic was abolished and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-the-maldives">Sultanate of the Maldives</a> was restored in 1954.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-maldivian-republic.jpg" alt="First Maldivian Republic" width="320" height="227"><figcaption>Image: Petrus Bertius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1598_Middleburg_Bertius_Maldives_map_latin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1953 CE – 1954 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Male</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mohamed Amin Didi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dhivehi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/maldives">Maldives</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Republic of the Maldives</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1954&amp;focus=first-maldivian-republic" aria-label="First Maldivian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6719 2021 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Maldivian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7039 2277L7039 2277M7039 2277L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7039 2277h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7039 2277h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7039 2277h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Male. <a href="/atlas?year=1954&amp;focus=first-maldivian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
